# No git restore until the owner says restore

Owner standing order (2026-08-09):

## Forbidden unless the owner types **restore** in that message

- Do **not** run `git restore`
- Do **not** run `git checkout <commit> -- <files>`
- Do **not** overwrite working files from an old commit / tag / branch tip
- Do **not** “put the app back” by wholesale reverting files from history

## Required instead

- Fix by **editing the current files in place** (smallest class / logic change)
- If icons/buttons moved, change only the positioning classes — do not pull whole screens from git history
- If unsure, **ask** — do not restore

## Exception

Only when the owner explicitly says **restore** (or clear equivalent: “restore from commit …”, “checkout that file from …”) in the **same** message.

Default: **edit in place. No git restore.**
